        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Sub-Saharan Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Mansa Musa</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1280 CE – c. 1337 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1280; the date is unknown, but he appears to have been a young man in 1324; of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keita-dynasty">Keita dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, a descendant of Abu Bakr, brother of Sunjata, though his parentage is disputed</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1337; the date is uncertain: 1332 or earlier by some reckonings, 1337 regarded as most likely by Nehemia Levtzion; place and manner are not recorded</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Ninth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansa">Mansa</a> (ruler) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>, from the early 1300s until his death</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajj">hajj</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in 1324–1325; lavish gifts of gold in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>; bringing Gao and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>; recruiting scholars such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-ishaq-al-sahili">Abu Ishaq al-Sahili</a>; building in Timbuktu, including part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djinguereber-mosque">Djinguereber Mosque</a>; a lasting reputation for fabulous wealth</span></div>
        </div>
